  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="37196f7c-8986-5a87-8b89-9485b70179a0" activityNameId="db553526-066a-57f7-824c-4844c200242f" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Epichlorohydrin, from hypochlorination of allyl chloride, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Epichlorohydrin, from hypochlorination of allyl chloride, at plant
Allyl chloride is reacted  with hylochlorous acid and calcium chloride to produce epichlorohydrin, calcium chloride and water;
Synonyms: 1-chloro-2,3-epoxyporpane, chloromethyl-oxirane, 1,2-epoxy-3-chloropropan; 
UUID: e5750fb3-9b49-38a8-89ee-3ac12d97b0a5
Multi-output process that produces 1 kg epichlorohydrin,  l.375 kg calcium chloride, and 18 kg of trichloropropane at plant. Economic allocation with allocation factor of 82.4% to epichlorohydrin, 16.2% to calcium chloride, and 1.4% to trichloropropane..
Location: RER
Technology: based on industry data in the US
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature data 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_e5750fb3-9b49-38a8-89ee-3ac12d97b0a5.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
